25
00:01:23,800 --> 00:01:29,680
Language Takeaway Our first word today is the name of this job.

26
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,370
The person is called a handyman.

27
00:01:31,690 --> 00:01:33,250
Okay, so that's a profession.

28
00:01:33,690 --> 00:01:34,890
You are a handyman.

29
00:01:35,090 --> 00:01:37,410
Now what exactly does a handyman do?

30
00:01:37,810 --> 00:01:39,590
Well, a handyman fixes things.

31
00:01:40,050 --> 00:01:42,850
He is usually a generalist.

32
00:01:43,390 --> 00:01:47,240
He fixes things all over the house, not just the bathroom or the kitchen.

33
00:01:47,820 --> 00:01:51,260
So he can just fix things that are a little bit broken.

34
00:01:51,660 --> 00:02:03,420
But if, for example, your car needs a new radiator or it needs a new important part, maybe you would take the car to someone who is more experienced with cars.

35
00:02:03,900 --> 00:02:07,220
But in the case of a handyman, if anything is broken, he can generally fix it.

36
00:02:07,420 --> 00:02:17,920
Okay, so as Catherine explained, basically a handyman just does any type or many types of general work of things that may be broken around the house or the office.

37
00:02:18,290 --> 00:02:20,790
We had a couple of examples of these in today's dialogue, didn't we?

38
00:02:20,890 --> 00:02:21,570
What was that first one?

39
00:02:21,800 --> 00:02:22,800
Kind of gross.

40
00:02:22,800 --> 00:02:30,490
Yeah, well, he had to fix the air conditioning, but then he also had to fix the bathroom toilet because it kept clogging up.

41
00:02:31,010 --> 00:02:34,470
Okay, so a toilet gets clogged up.

42
00:02:35,000 --> 00:02:36,050
To clog up.

43
00:02:36,760 --> 00:02:37,310
What does this mean?

44
00:02:37,840 --> 00:02:45,130
So it means that something is blocking the way of the water being able to go out.

45
00:02:45,760 --> 00:02:47,030
So the water doesn't go down.

46
00:02:48,040 --> 00:02:57,400
And sometimes if the toilet is really clogged and someone tries to flush the toilet again, the water comes onto the floor and it's very dirty and very gross.

47
00:02:57,400 --> 00:02:57,630
That's right.

48
00:02:58,400 --> 00:03:05,890
So actually, maybe sometimes in the kitchen, pieces of food may fall into the sink and it may clog up the sink.

49
00:03:06,350 --> 00:03:10,710
Okay, so to clog up means to block or to get in the way of.

50
00:03:10,930 --> 00:03:11,430
That's right.

51
00:03:11,950 --> 00:03:18,730
And apart from the toilets being clogged up, he also may have to take a look at the circuit breakers.

52
00:03:19,120 --> 00:03:22,520
All right, so this is not about water or about plumbing.

53
00:03:23,280 --> 00:03:24,980
Circuit breakers have to do with electricity.

54
00:03:26,120 --> 00:03:33,360
And in this case, that box in your apartment or near your apartment that controls the different circuits.

55
00:03:33,380 --> 00:03:41,830
So sometimes if the lights go out, you know that you have to check the circuit breaker and make sure that the circuits are all working properly.

56
00:03:42,330 --> 00:03:42,750
That's right.

57
00:03:43,110 --> 00:03:49,110
So the circuit breakers are kind of like a protection from too much electricity and that's why they go out.

58
00:03:49,810 --> 00:03:58,370
And now for our final word on language takeaway, something that also got clogged up at their office, we're talking about the gutters.

59
00:03:58,440 --> 00:04:05,120
All right, so many people's houses have gutters or sometimes an office building will have gutters.

60
00:04:05,120 --> 00:04:12,720
These are trays on the roof of a house or a building that will catch the water when it rains.

61
00:04:13,400 --> 00:04:20,520
Because you know, sometimes rainwater can be very, very heavy and it's dangerous on your house, on the roof of your house because it can hurt the roof.

62
00:04:21,360 --> 00:04:26,660
But if it comes into this gutter, into this little tray, then it will come down and fall on the ground.

63
00:04:27,080 --> 00:04:29,040
So these are a way to protect your roof.

64
00:04:29,040 --> 00:04:33,200
But these often get clogged up with leaves and with garbage.

65
00:04:33,620 --> 00:04:34,120
That's right.

66
00:04:34,620 --> 00:04:43,400
So they're like small little ways or little roads, if you want to call them, where the water can go and escape and go into a specific place.

67
00:04:44,360 --> 00:04:46,960
We have them on the sides of roads as well, many times.

68
00:04:47,310 --> 00:04:53,130
So gutters that you find on the ground, sometimes you find them on the roof of a house, but those are a little bit different.

69
00:04:53,590 --> 00:04:58,590
The gutters on the ground are basically pathways for water to come down.

70
00:04:58,750 --> 00:05:04,950
Because if there's no gutter, then all of the water is on the road and it can flood very quickly.

71
00:05:05,050 --> 00:05:05,450
That's right.

72
00:05:06,520 --> 00:05:13,400
And so this is a way for the water and even the garbage to go on the side of the road and not be in the way of the cars.

73
00:05:13,400 --> 00:05:14,400
That's right.

74
00:05:14,400 --> 00:05:18,700
You see them on highways and roads very often because you don't want the road filled with water.

75
00:05:19,400 --> 00:05:24,560
So these gutters are a small path where all the water will fall into it and escape safely from the highway.

76
00:05:25,360 --> 00:05:25,560
That's right.

77
00:05:26,360 --> 00:05:27,360
All right.

