00:06:27,730 --> 00:06:32,130
Well, this first phrase is a phrase that I like to use and I do use it very often.

97
00:06:33,190 --> 00:06:36,190
We heard that Dan is on top of that.

98
00:06:37,490 --> 00:06:41,490
We need to call a handyman in here and he says, nope, Dan is on top of that.

99
00:06:42,050 --> 00:06:44,210
To be on top of something, what does it mean?

100
00:06:44,970 --> 00:06:53,330
When she says Dan is on top of that, she's basically saying Dan is taking care of this or Dan is already calling the handyman to come and fix it.

101
00:06:53,910 --> 00:06:56,770
You are aware of the problem and you're trying to solve it.

102
00:06:57,060 --> 00:06:58,420
Okay, so don't worry.

103
00:06:58,900 --> 00:07:00,320
You don't have to call the handyman.

104
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,900
Dan is on top of that.

105
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:03,040
Dan will call him.

106
00:07:03,400 --> 00:07:04,400
Right.

107
00:07:04,400 --> 00:07:07,320
So to be on top of something is to make sure that something is done.

108
00:07:07,440 --> 00:07:13,560
So you could say, you know, Marco, I really, I hope you stay on top of that project because it's very important.

109
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:14,180
Right.

110
00:07:14,480 --> 00:07:17,020
Or don't worry, the report will be finished on time.

111
00:07:17,380 --> 00:07:18,240
I am on top of that.

112
00:07:18,520 --> 00:07:18,680
Great.

113
00:07:19,520 --> 00:07:20,520
All right.

114
00:07:20,520 --> 00:07:32,600
Now moving on to our next phrase, they were talking about all the problems that this office has and the person said, well, they might as well ask the handyman to also fix the electrical wiring.

115
00:07:32,600 --> 00:07:32,860
