He might as well also fix electrical wiring.

122
00:07:51,040 --> 00:07:51,160
Right.

123
00:07:51,160 --> 00:07:59,460
So taking advantage of the fact that you are already doing something or you are already here, you can start doing something else as well.

124
00:07:59,900 --> 00:08:04,120
Or maybe we could say this in a different context to like, you know, we're going to order a pizza for lunch.

125
00:08:04,780 --> 00:08:08,400
You know what, Marco might as well order two because there are so many people here.

126
00:08:08,620 --> 00:08:08,800
Right.

127
00:08:09,180 --> 00:08:14,640
So taking advantage of the fact that we are ordering pizza, we might as well get more for everyone.

128
00:08:15,080 --> 00:08:15,260
Okay.

129
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:24,880
And for our last phrase, when they mentioned all the work that has to be done, they said the handyman definitely has his work cut out for him.

130
00:08:25,410 --> 00:08:25,770
Okay.

131
00:08:25,770 --> 00:08:30,810
So if someone has his work cut out for him, it means that he has a lot of work to do.

132
00:08:31,110 --> 00:08:31,430
That's right.

133
