159
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:53,720
So a handyman is also commonly referred to as a jack of all trades.

160
00:09:54,420 --> 00:09:54,840
That's right.

161
00:09:55,640 --> 00:09:57,280
So these are both kind of funny words.

162
00:09:57,280 --> 00:10:01,600
First of all, handy as an adjective means useful or helpful.

163
00:10:01,600 --> 00:10:03,820
So maybe a hammer is a handy tool.

164
00:10:04,200 --> 00:10:08,620
It's a very handy tool or I find my iPhone has some very handy applications.

165
00:10:08,960 --> 00:10:09,860
I can use the dictionary.

166
00:10:11,240 --> 00:10:12,960
So a handyman is someone who's helpful.

167
00:10:13,000 --> 00:10:13,800
He can do many things.

168
00:10:14,080 --> 00:10:22,720
But a jack of all trades is very special because it means he is a person that can do basically any job.

169
00:10:22,720 --> 00:10:23,720
Right.

170
00:10:23,720 --> 00:10:29,190
So sometimes in offices, people may have someone that they may refer to as a jack of all trades.

171
00:10:29,480 --> 00:10:30,930
So he may fix the computers.

172
00:10:31,470 --> 00:10:37,250
He also knows a little bit about marketing and does many odd and random things around the office.

173
00:10:37,590 --> 00:10:37,910
That's right.

174
00:10:38,880 --> 00:10:41,480
You could say my friend Paul, he's a jack of all trades.

175
00:10:41,480 --> 00:10:42,710
He can fix a car.

176
00:10:42,980 --> 00:10:43,690
He can cook.

177
00:10:44,440 --> 00:10:49,560
He can fix a door or a window, but he can also sew.

178
00:10:49,560 --> 00:10:50,680
So he's a jack of all trades.

179
00:10:50,810 --> 00:10:51,690
He has many, many skills.

180
00:10:52,210 --> 00:10:52,430
That's right.

181
00:10:53,280 --> 00:10:57,000
And talking about these skills, being a handyman is not a profession per se.

182
00:10:57,000 --> 00:10:57,840
It's actually a trade.

183
00:10:58,450 --> 00:10:58,890
That's right.

184
00:10:59,090 --> 00:11:05,310
And so we say this because it's something that you normally do with your hands and you don't have to go to university to study it.

185
00:11:05,330 --> 00:11:09,010
You maybe have an apprenticeship where you study by working.

186
00:11:09,990 --> 00:11:15,670
And it's one of a few very, very important trades like being a plumber or an electrician.

187
00:11:16,150 --> 00:11:17,610
But a handyman is more general.

188
00:11:18,000 --> 00:11:19,920
Like we said, you can do many different things.

189
00:11:19,920 --> 00:11:20,110
That's right.

190
00:11:20,920 --> 00:11:21,410
So very interesting.

191
00:11:21,920 --> 00:11:23,070
There are many trades out there.

192
00:11:23,320 --> 00:11:26,710
Maybe you can come on the site and mention some of these that you may know.

193
00:11:26,840 --> 00:11:31,950
